design.prefetcher_source:
#include <cstdint>
#include "address.h"
#include "modules.h"

struct gen_default_s1 : public champsim::modules::prefetcher {
  using prefetcher::prefetcher;

  // State for the stride prefetcher
  champsim::block_number last_demand_block = champsim::block_number{0}; // Stores the block address of the last demand access
  bool has_last_demand = false;                                          // Flag to indicate if last_demand_block is valid
  champsim::block_number::difference_type current_stride = 0;           // The stride detected between consecutive demand accesses
  int stride_consecutive_count = 0;                                      // How many times the current_stride has been observed consecutively

  uint32_t prefetcher_cache_operate(champsim::address addr, champsim::address ip,
                                     uint8_t cache_hit, bool useful_prefetch,
                                     access_type type, uint32_t metadata_in) {
    // Only train on demand accesses (LOAD, RFO, WRITE). Prefetches should not influence training.
    if (type == access_type::PREFETCH) {
      return metadata_in;
    }

    champsim::block_number current_block{addr};

    if (has_last_demand) {
      // Calculate the stride between the last demand access and the current demand access
      champsim::block_number::difference_type detected_stride = champsim::offset(last_demand_block, current_block);

      if (detected_stride == 0) {
        // The same block was accessed again, or no movement. Reset stride detection.
        stride_consecutive_count = 0;
        current_stride = 0; // Reset current_stride to indicate no active stride
      } else {
        if (detected_stride == current_stride) {
          // The same stride was detected again, increase confidence
          stride_consecutive_count++;
        } else {
          // A new stride was detected, reset confidence and update the current_stride
          current_stride = detected_stride;
          stride_consecutive_count = 1; // This is the first occurrence of this new stride
        }

        // If we've seen the same stride at least twice (meaning three consecutive blocks
        // have formed a consistent stride: A, A+S, A+2S), then we are confident to prefetch.
        // On the A+2S access, stride_consecutive_count becomes 2, triggering the prefetch for A+3S.
        if (stride_consecutive_count >= 2) {
          champsim::block_number pf_blk = current_block + current_stride;
          // Issue a prefetch for the next block in the detected stride pattern
          prefetch_line(champsim::address{pf_blk}, true, metadata_in);
        }
      }
    } else {
      // This is the very first demand access observed. Initialize the state.
      has_last_demand = true;
    }

    // Update last_demand_block for the next access to this cache
    last_demand_block = current_block;

    return metadata_in;
  }

  uint32_t prefetcher_cache_fill(champsim::address addr, long set, long way,
                                  uint8_t prefetch, champsim::address evicted_addr,
                                  uint32_t metadata_in) {
    // This prefetcher does not require any action or training on cache fill events.
    return metadata_in;
  }
};

provenance.prompt_text:
Target simulator: ChampSim (the fork shipped in ghcr.io/ucb-bar/chia-champsim,
base revision 164fdb1ed01185a21a39c292937bf26bb7f4c694).

The module must be one C++ struct that derives from the prefetcher module API:

  #include <cstdint>
  #include "address.h"
  #include "modules.h"

  struct <NAME> : public champsim::modules::prefetcher {
    using prefetcher::prefetcher;

    uint32_t prefetcher_cache_operate(champsim::address addr, champsim::address ip,
                                       uint8_t cache_hit, bool useful_prefetch,
                                       access_type type, uint32_t metadata_in) {
      // called on every core-cache access; the real signature is
      // prefetch_line(champsim::address pf_addr, bool fill_this_level, uint32_t prefetch_metadata)
      return metadata_in;
    }

    uint32_t prefetcher_cache_fill(champsim::address addr, long set, long way,
                                    uint8_t prefetch, champsim::address evicted_addr,
                                    uint32_t metadata_in) {
      // called on a fill into the cache being modelled
      return metadata_in;
    }
  };

Constraints: standard library only, no external packages, no template
parameters, no file or network I/O, state kept in plain member fields.

Hard API constraints for this revision. Each of these was a real compiler error
observed in a generated candidate, so re-read the code for them before answering:

- champsim::address is a typed bit-slice, not an integer. static_cast<int64_t>(addr),
  addr + 1 and addr >> n all fail to compile.
- Convert once, at the top of the callback: champsim::block_number blk{addr};
  All line arithmetic happens on blk, which is an integer-like type.
- Convert back when issuing a prefetch:
  prefetch_line(champsim::address{blk + 1}, true, metadata_in);
- Distance between two lines uses champsim::offset(a, b) on block_number
  operands, and yields champsim::block_number::difference_type (signed).
- LOG2_BLOCK_SIZE is an unsigned int, so it cannot shift an address; shift
  plain integers only.
- Key tables on champsim::address or champsim::block_number values, which
  support == and <. There is no address-to-integer conversion to hash with.
- champsim::block_number is not an integer either: it supports ==, <, ++, and
  addition/subtraction of a difference_type, but there is no operator%, operator/
  or operator>> on it, so you cannot index an array with an address or mask off
  region bits. To reason about a region, hold a champsim::block_number base and
  take champsim::offset(base, blk), which returns a signed line count you can
  compare or use as an offset. Track a small fixed set of registers, or a
  std::vector of entries scanned with ==, instead of an address-indexed table.
- Include what you use: <vector>, <algorithm>, <cstddef> are available; anything
  else is not.

Name the struct exactly `gen_default_s1`.

Design brief (seed 1): Design a novel L2 software-transparent prefetcher that trains on demand accesses and issues at most one prefetch per access.

Return only one ```cpp fenced block holding the complete module, including the three #include lines. No prose, no comments describing the plan.

